text:
The \textbf{orthogonal projection of \( \vec{v} \) into the line
spanned by a nonzero \( \vec{s}\, \)}
 is this vector.
\begin{equation*}
 \proj{\vec{v}}{\spanof{\vec{s}\,}}=
 \frac{ \vec{v}\dotprod\vec{s} }{ \vec{s}\dotprod\vec{s} }\cdot\vec{s}
\end{equation*}

