text:
In \( \mathbb{R}^3 \), the orthogonal projection of a general vector
\begin{equation*}
 \begin{pmatrix}x \\ y \\ z\end{pmatrix}
\end{equation*}
into the \( y \)-axis is
\begin{equation*}
 \frac{ \begin{pmatrix}x \\ y \\ z\end{pmatrix}\dotprod\begin{pmatrix}0 \\ 1 \\ 0\end{pmatrix} }{
 \begin{pmatrix}0 \\ 1 \\ 0\end{pmatrix}\dotprod\begin{pmatrix}0 \\ 1 \\ 0\end{pmatrix} }
 \cdot\begin{pmatrix}0 \\ 1 \\ 0\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}0 \\ y \\ 0\end{pmatrix}
\end{equation*}
which matches our intuitive expectation.

