text:
The matrix \textbf{adjoint}
(or \textbf{adjugate})
to the square matrix \( T \) 
(or the \textbf{classical adjoint}) 
is
\begin{equation*}
 \adj(T)=
 \begin{pmatrix}
 T_{1,1} &T_{2,1} &\ldots &T_{n,1} \\
 T_{1,2} &T_{2,2} &\ldots &T_{n,2} \\
 &\vdots & & \\
 T_{1,n} &T_{2,n} &\ldots &T_{n,n}
 \end{pmatrix}
\end{equation*}
where the row \( i \), column \( j \) entry, \( T_{j,i} \), 
is the \( j,i \) cofactor.

