text:
The \textbf{orthogonal complement\/}
of a subspace \( M \) of $\mathbb{R}^n$ is
\begin{equation*}
 M^\perp=\set{\vec{v}\in\mathbb{R}^n\suchthat
 \vec{v} \text{ is perpendicular to all vectors in }M}
\end{equation*}
(read ``\( M \) perp'').
The 
\textbf{orthogonal projection}
 \( \proj{\vec{v}\,}{M} \) 
of a vector is its projection into $M$ along \( M^\perp \).

