text:
In a vector space with basis $B$
the \textbf{representation of \( \vec{v} \) with respect to \( B \)}
 is
the column vector of the coefficients used to express $\vec{v}$ as a 
linear combination of the basis vectors:
\begin{equation*}
 \rep{\vec{v}}{B}
 =
 \begin{pmatrix}c_1 \\ c_2 \\ \vdots \\ c_n\end{pmatrix}_{B}
\end{equation*}
where
\( B=\sequence{\vec{\beta}_1,\dots,\vec{\beta}_n} \) and 
\( \vec{v}=\lincombo{c}{\vec{\beta}} \).
The \( c \)'s are the
\textbf{coordinates of \( \vec{v} \) with respect to \( B \)}
.

