\begin{equation*}
 a_0+a_1x+\cdots+a_nx^n
 \mapsunder{d/dx}
 a_1+2a_2x+3a_3x^2+\cdots+na_nx^{n-1}
\end{equation*}
is a linear transformation as this result from calculus shows:
\( d(c_1f+c_2g)/dx=c_1\,(df/dx)+c_2\,(dg/dx) \).

